## Files

| File | Runs on | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `rpi_agent.py` | **Pi** | Headless agent. JSON commands on stdin, telemetry on stdout. |
| `robstride_gui/remote_worker.py` | Laptop | ControlWorker-shaped proxy over the pipe. |
| `main.py` | Laptop | `--remote` and `--remote-path`. |
| `robstride_gui/ui/main_window.py` | Laptop | The three edits above. |
| `publish.py` | Laptop | Standalone one-motor panel. Imports nothing from `robstride_gui`. |

### Keep `rpi_agent.py` in git

It runs on the Pi, so it is easy to leave it living only on the SD card — outside
version control, with no way to tell from the laptop which version is deployed.
Keep the laptop copy as the source of truth and treat the Pi's as a deployment:

```bash
rsync -av rpi_agent.py usvz@rs04pi.local:~/Desktop/Robstride_Control_Gui/
```

There is no version check at runtime. Edit on the laptop, forget to push, and
you will be running the old agent and wondering why a fix did not take.

