## Known limitations

- **The port dropdown lists the laptop's CAN interfaces, not the Pi's.** With no
  local CAN hardware it falls back to `can0`-`can4`, which happens to match a
  RobStride hub — so picking `can4` works by coincidence, not detection.
- **The Scan range is not remembered**, so it defaults to 0-127 each session.
- **`publish.py` drives one motor at a time**, by design.
- **`_comm_failures` is shared across buses**, so a dead adapter can still tear
  down a healthy one.
- **A blocking enable stalls every bus.** Command handling runs on the control
  thread, so an enable or mode-switch starves all buses. `_feed_other_motors`
  must therefore stay.
- **Setpoints cross the network at UI rate, not 100 Hz.** Deliberate, but it
  means fast externally-generated trajectories should be executed on the Pi
  rather than streamed frame by frame.